[{"id":"VRCE-1-28-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of Rāma of measureless prowess, who had asked the question, the highly energetic Viśvāmitra answered, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.825,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a8968c68291743c7eba37d5bd941b2ba88397a41395fa71553c582ed19cfbd87","compact":"ff86cef072dbc59b348e532f84aa43654b738c367ddcbfc7bf113f60b7c6ce4a","nasal":"ff86cef072dbc59b348e532f84aa43654b738c367ddcbfc7bf113f60b7c6ce4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":2,"english":"Here, O mighty-armed Rama, Visnu of mighty asceticism worshipped of all the deities, for years upon years, and hundreds of Yugas, dwelt for carrying on his austerities and Yoga. This, O Rāma, was formerly the hermitage of the high-souled Vāmana. And this famed as Siddhāśrama, in consequence of that one of potent asceticism having attained fruition there. And it came to pass that at this time Virocana's son, king Välī; having vanquished the celestials with Indra and the Maruts, established that dominion of his, famous in the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-2","DUTT-1-29-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c6e6009091ef5185e090249f5363018402b6555316fcf8abd9310273095e364","compact":"e233104dc99a6397a3968ec3e37944cca263461afa9696a456c2060ac2f33dce","nasal":"e233104dc99a6397a3968ec3e37944cca263461afa9696a456c2060ac2f33dce"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":3,"english":"And this famed as Siddhāśrama, in consequence of that one of potent asceticism having attained fruition there. And it came to pass that at this time Virocana's son, king Välī; having vanquished the celestials with Indra and the Maruts, established that dominion of his, famous in the three worlds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.79,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43db40297e19a2d84b4aea464085464e878228e4e7f49c840d2fc35e46f863c8","compact":"c7f64543d7eac963a177b37560600052ad270a8e9a306f07a04c61510869ac2d","nasal":"02230c18fddd1f408debfb42f990e373929a221441b5dd98143c909bdf802d51"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":4,"english":"And that mighty chief of the Asuras celebrated a sacrifice. And as Vāli was performing that sacrifice, the deities with Agni at their head, coming to Vişnu himself at this asylum, addressed him saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"483a5e2a171d40698d83b1cdbe1c753621293dda127dcfb743567b0734965ea0","compact":"eda1d38b1fd7b5bd2531559bcb4be516887fb3a99c3caaedef2c6aad6cc48ac3","nasal":"eda1d38b1fd7b5bd2531559bcb4be516887fb3a99c3caaedef2c6aad6cc48ac3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":5,"english":"Virocana's son, Vali, O Visnu, is celebrating a sacrifice. Do you, before the ceremony is finished, accomplish your own end.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3f9fce20d384dc75ffc6b99a397e448bd3ef506c4e7a0a5915d4f2167d2b7609","compact":"9bd95477beffb488c97e13fd63f591cfd0f3fe1724eef13349ecb8b1cd81f3ac","nasal":"9bd95477beffb488c97e13fd63f591cfd0f3fe1724eef13349ecb8b1cd81f3ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":6,"english":"He duly confer upon such as repair to him from various quarters all those things that they ask for. And do yourself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"27d426955c1e13fb009c6c88a75ee61aeb5e7f7565d0510914ced74681a46941","compact":"590ca9a0c4a556b56c03d44db8492d8d67fd5dd2cb8240cda78e45258746beda","nasal":"3d7c6e70e03ec3414f696788dacb7351b9a33fd2ab1fe896a4cb855a18379f49"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":7,"english":"O Visnu, aided by your power of illusion, assuming a Dwarf form, accomplish the welfare of the gods.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"698dea83f2b146076ba6c3eeced01321497f24b61b72cd6acb3906d7222d590f","compact":"3a3daa03aa4a2df57e68fd9670afde09c1a16679cbaf27b596ab8c245ad731bd","nasal":"3a3daa03aa4a2df57e68fd9670afde09c1a16679cbaf27b596ab8c245ad731bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":8,"english":"And this place through your grace will attain the name of Siddhasrama. The work, O lord of the celestials, has been accomplished.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.921,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"548611b5b4887ed91e20fbc64c44ebbc947a15dded4085dad181c6cab552a66a","compact":"de9fcbad59eadae5dd0acdef32a4e53afd0482496839fd2f9622d4a72ffc5049","nasal":"e1dcd51342e8f3f670042c9076befbe5bb41e7c680e7196cb0dcf27fe5c2a82a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":9,"english":"Do you now, O you of the six attributes, ascend from hence! And accordingly Vişnu of mighty energy took his birth in Aditi. And assuming the form of a dwarf, he presented himself before Virocana's son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ab4b6694b64f227cc2d4292322182a25af926b9ddf2d88d30f09a82b9bd50a6","compact":"0b1e18dd61d266550d3ace31103a332d39fabf6b855dbaf2e613db488303e64e","nasal":"0b1e18dd61d266550d3ace31103a332d39fabf6b855dbaf2e613db488303e64e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":10,"english":"And then asking for as much earth as could be covered by three footsteps, that one ever engaged in the welfare of all creatures; with the object of compassing the good of all, stood occupying the worlds. And having by his power restrained Bali, that one of exceeding energy, again conferred the three worlds upon the mighty Indra, and made them subject to his control.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.426,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a4936b8b3986480b7b1bd13517768c4e0af25f69c29fe25b5da2d8c44f50339f","compact":"9d7266d299b3311c4ae28093604f131af39ae2952cd50ee592a79b22ff2fb5b5","nasal":"9d7266d299b3311c4ae28093604f131af39ae2952cd50ee592a79b22ff2fb5b5"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":11,"english":"And then asking for as much earth as could be covered by three footsteps, that one ever engaged in the welfare of all creatures; with the object of compassing the good of all, stood occupying the worlds. And having by his power restrained Bali, that one of exceeding energy, again conferred the three worlds upon the mighty Indra, and made them subject to his control.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b77d796eadcb1471169174e4cd2a7725b2a8de217d5b3cd5df67224289192ac","compact":"4b2871c56c5e84d5ecbb874e28619efadcf8c220530dc48d75ec1d8a2fbcec47","nasal":"8a0a8f8f172c41c66b0547f8b6dead86576a1ac08ce6ef0c0177b55b49475503"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":12,"english":"Formerly he used to dwell in this asylum capable of removing fatigue. And hermitage is infested by Raksasas disturbing rites. And, O most puissant of men, here you should slay those ones of wicked ways.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.787,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e62e0232ef98af695495a991708c79f9892f4623495b4916be89a67ad75692aa","compact":"4317f9e9ce7bb00e3560b20e7c88fcd07f567b49a0cf2e6294f5ca0d3da8a0a5","nasal":"62204c1a0e0aa93874a396fd98513493390bfccfd3d7bb49835515e38a8d29d1"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":13,"english":"Formerly he used to dwell in this asylum capable of removing fatigue. And hermitage is infested by Raksasas disturbing rites. And, O most puissant of men, here you should slay those ones of wicked ways.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.969,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5538448d381c017b238b70eb5843cf8296c69f87bd5482746f60a0b4463d2292","compact":"d7ac00ac25192904d90a16d5d43682ff5973a0e1167c6e5ac5cff3e367b469d4","nasal":"462bc997f97eceea359dff3cd6a78d608174f428d4ef5023d72b915d46543512"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":14,"english":"To-day, O Rama, will I repair to this supremely excellent Siddhāśrama. And this asylum, child, is as much your as mine.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b7e7aa68e8a0e3a6a002a3e5f07cf47c3aa21b833f1e19725ecebd48f4bc76ab","compact":"d7ff278a3a98659710e2b187b76941a1714f6fcb079bc74253ba5e70cce5db64","nasal":"d7ff278a3a98659710e2b187b76941a1714f6fcb079bc74253ba5e70cce5db64"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":15,"english":"And beholding Viśvāmitra, the ascetics inhabiting Siddhāśrama, suddenly rising in joy, worshipped that intelligent one, and extended to the princes the rites of hospitality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da7abac538674a99cdf9aab95d0526d1b07bd65a4bd8b4aa7938fcf23f8bed17","compact":"69962ce98a879be53af6252715f3b6e25400f93bbc3e72b1c10dff43d0c00bb3","nasal":"69962ce98a879be53af6252715f3b6e25400f93bbc3e72b1c10dff43d0c00bb3"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":16,"english":"And beholding Viśvāmitra, the ascetics inhabiting Siddhāśrama, suddenly rising in joy, worshipped that intelligent one, and extended to the princes the rites of hospitality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.956,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e177fe8c118a5d7fea039c7df98326b393b7353ed903b844a88439ca43a20ae","compact":"a4f3adc9f83d5352b348ce23d84ed28fa984389756105da1b6d9d3645c9f1941","nasal":"f7a023cb373e6d8b181faa95c51745d8aae4c803a08f662f931f541def3e309c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":17,"english":"And then having reposed for a while, those unreproved princes, the descendants of Raghu, with clasped hands, addressed that foremost of ascetics.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7e0ea67098d9b9c92a423a2b474c3c3b8abe0926bd07e635637e43c1e9c078f9","compact":"8402a62d5dbfbf07132aea0cb02b6ee835fc55091a789190e4ef8d3f9217d603","nasal":"74f4bcbbd5c34e0b467d180106048fab9c440899c8a2c683134353b4b21e87d9"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":18,"english":"Be you even to-day initiated to the ceremony. Good betide you, O best of ascetics! Let this Siddhāśrama verily attain fruition, and let your words be verified!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"401ce71ca38c39837322860fc78330873d3d8e6b02dc94889f36b29c3c66ffc8","compact":"9d26f90ce644ec5b76661a81abd61cdc75169e6211ca1d51c0ad9d33ed212d3f","nasal":"9d26f90ce644ec5b76661a81abd61cdc75169e6211ca1d51c0ad9d33ed212d3f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":19,"english":"Thus addressed, that mighty saint of exceeding energy, observing vows, and with his senses under restraint, caused himself to be initiated into the ceremony. And like to the Kumāras, (Skanda and Visakha) Rāma and Laksmana, having passed the night pleasantly, rose in the morning, and having finished their morning worship, and with purity and selfrestraint recited the prime mantras, paid their obeisance to the sacrificial fire and the sacrificer, Viśvāmitra, who was seated.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.906,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d0c29ab33def80f7a3ddfe8e220cea96fad0f94ae036be1fbdf7e7fdda64fa57","compact":"05a39054c8a373b961489a421c828742ed75bd67377f22936a8f1d6a849b5fb1","nasal":"975b4e96341eebdcf7fae883f5f1f2836c251e3a4b76951b1c2bf562c805f146"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-28-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":28,"verse":20,"english":"Thus addressed, that mighty saint of exceeding energy, observing vows, and with his senses under restraint, caused himself to be initiated into the ceremony. And like to the Kumāras, (Skanda and Visakha) Rāma and Laksmana, having passed the night pleasantly, rose in the morning, and having finished their morning worship, and with purity and selfrestraint recited the prime mantras, paid their obeisance to the sacrificial fire and the sacrificer, Viśvāmitra, who was seated.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.954,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-29-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1028020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5774f14d240cf7e24c0120dd7a1d0b3e1b8733cc7e2effed1ea997577aed9e8c","compact":"2ccf392d517c85068edf24d63a8aef4